## Lore

Mantis Men come from human stock, not insects. The name describes the body:
very tall and thin, with stilt legs, long spindly arms and fingers, a long neck
and a wedge-shaped head, hairless but for a little fuzz on the forearms and
jaw. They move slowly with their arms folded, and sway from side to side when
something catches their attention, much like the insect.

They are no stealthy predators. Mantis Men are scholars and wandering
philosophers, stuffed with lore, science and their own observations. Where the
Beast Men and Metal Morphs study machines, the Mantis Men study everything else,
coolly and with an eye for the esoteric. They doubt the Shamans'' talk of a
chosen people, but are certain they outrank ordinary humans, and like the
Leopard Men they want a harder line against invaders.

For all their thoughtfulness they are close to sociopathic, detached from
humans and other intelligent races, and feel kinship only with fellow mutants.

## Mutant Shaman

Any sizable clan is led by a Shaman, and a Mantis Man may be one. The **Mantis
Man Shaman** variant carries the Shaman''s attribute and P.P.E. gains and adds
the Shaman skills. What the app does not do for it:

- The Shaman skills **replace all Secondary Skills, all Piloting skills and all
  modern W.P.s**. A Shaman never uses a modern weapon, vehicle or machine. Drop
  those picks by hand.
- **Commune with the Mighty Lady.** The Shamans now worship Isis and may pray to
  her. A *prayer of strength* is heard on 01-20%, +5% per level: it gives +6 to
  P.S., +1D4x10 M.D.C. and 48 hours without food or water, and may be tried six
  times a year. A *prayer of inspiration or wisdom* is heard on 01-12%, +3% per
  level (+10% after a week of fasting) and answers with a dream vision of
  insight, an idea or a warning.
- **The Shaman levels on its own ladder**, the Gateway Knight & Mutant Shaman
  table on printed 79: 0, 2,351, 4,701, 9,401, 18,801, 28,001, 38,001, 53,001,
  77,001, 102,001, 143,001, 195,201, 240,401, 310,601, 360,801.

Shamans are also the lawmakers, judges and leaders of their clans.

## GM Notes

Mantis Men value technology and magic and distrust both. More than any other
mutant they roam Madhaven and beyond watching other peoples, so where most
mutants turn up in groups of 1D6+2, a Mantis Man is met alone, in a pair, or in
another race''s company. The Leopard Men are their closest friends among the
mutants. They are fascinated by the Splugorth and their minions and suspect the
Shemarrians are artificial. They dislike Horune Pirates, Barbarians and bullies,
though they deal with them when it pays. They count as enemies any outsider or invader, ghosts and the Undead Horrors, monsters, magical creatures and madmen. They live
wherever there are people to watch, above or below ground, and need few
comforts.

Height is 12-14 feet (3.6-4.3 m), though the hunch makes them look about
10 feet (3 m); weight 180 to 240 lbs (81 to 108 kg). They live about 90 years,
some to 125, and males outlive females by 10 to 20 years. Horror Factor rises
to 13 for two or more. Average NPC level is 1D6+4; a player character starts
at level one.

The Eastside Mantis Men are quietly building camps outside Madhaven with the
Guardia Leopard Men; the Leopard Men entry has the numbers.
', 'published', 'data-script'
WHERE NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM imported_classes WHERE class_id = 'mantis-men');


-- Read the result back rather than trusting the exit code. d1-apply prints
-- these, and a CR in the stored markdown means the checkout mangled the file.
SELECT class_id, name, status, length(markdown) AS bytes, instr(markdown, char(13)) > 0 AS has_cr
  FROM imported_classes WHERE class_id = 'mantis-men';

